    "body": "Problem:\r\nOnly the stdio channel can \"own\" a server (self-exit on close). After\r\n:restart the TUI reconnects over a socket, so the restarted server does\r\nnot have \"self-exit\" behavior when the channel closes (e.g. by UI\r\ndisconnect, host-terminal close, etc.), which leaves a dangling server.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n- Introduce `nvim_chan_set`. (`nvim_set_client_info` doesn't fit:\r\n  exposing it to Lua would require a `channel` param, which is not\r\n  backwards-compatible, plus it's awkward because it doesn't merge info.)\r\n- Broadcast per-channel properties in the \"restart\" UI event as an\r\n  opaque dict (a potentially useful pattern for other UI-events in the\r\n  future).\r\n  - UIs are expected to restore the channel properties on restart.\r\n- `nvim_get_chan_info()` reports \"detach\".\r\n- Remove `nvim__chan_set_detach()`.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n- fix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/42250\r\n- fix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/38807\r\n- ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/34399\r\n- ref https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/38456",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-09T11:41:58Z",
